			"Message": "fix(Wind): Correct userDataSync channel names in IPC stubs\n\nThe previous commit used incorrect IPC channel names for the userDataSync stubs:\n- `userDataSyncService` renamed to `userDataSync` (matches workbench/services/userDataSync/electron-browser/userDataSyncService.ts:13)\n- `userDataSync` renamed to `userDataSyncAccount` (matches userDataSyncIpc.ts:51)\n\nThe channel names now align with the actual VS Code IPC registration, ensuring calls route to the correct stub handlers.",
			"SHA": "671d83254b54b385da95e4e12d8acd7ec4d995e3"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T23:24:34Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1049,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Wind): Add IPC stubs for unimplemented VS Code services\n\nSeveral VS Code services invoked at runtime lack Mountain-side implementations,\ncausing IPC calls to return undefined. Downstream code then crashes when\nattempting operations like .forEach(), .map(), or destructuring on undefined.\n\nAdd stub handlers in TauriMainProcessService for:\n- extensionTipsService: Return empty arrays for recommendation queries\n- mcpManagement/mcpWorkbenchManagement: Return empty arrays for server lists\n- userDataSyncService: Return 'Uninitialised' status tuple [0, [], null]\n- userDataSync: Return undefined for account/not-signed-in state\n- userDataSyncStoreManagement: Return null\n- userDataAutoSync: Return undefined for trigger/turnOn/turnOff\n- languageDetection: Return null and empty extensions for detection\n\nThese stubs match the absence of corresponding backends in Land while\npreventing crashes in VS Code code paths that expect valid return shapes.",
			"SHA": "f0d6ccbe685fb74c28b788eedfd5533be49afb03"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T18:17:41Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1049,
				7
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Wind): Complete polyfill re-export migration in Wind Target\n\nComplete the migration of Wind polyfills to thin re-exports pointing to the canonical implementations in `@codeeditorland/output/Polyfill/`. The Target/Polyfills/ files are now minimal re-export proxies:\n\n- ChildProcessPolyfill.js\n- FileProtocolShim.js\n- FileSystemPolyfill.js\n- IPCRendererShim.js\n- NativeModulePolyfill.js\n- ProcessPolyfill.js\n- SharedProcessProxy.js\n\nThis follows the pattern established in the previous commit where implementations were moved to Output. Wind now maintains import path compatibility while delegating to the single source of truth. Fixes to polyfills should be made in Output, not Wind.",
			"SHA": "9bc98774e4e0c5c87bdbb926010d7663285f8a5c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T17:25:04Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1049,
				7
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Wind): Migrate polyfill implementations to Output as single source of truth\n\nReplace all Wind polyfill files with thin re-exports pointing to `@codeeditorland/output/Polyfill/`. The actual implementations have been moved to Output, eliminating duplicate code across the monorepo.\n\nAffected polyfills:\n- ChildProcessPolyfill, FileProtocolShim, FileSystemPolyfill\n- IPCRendererShim, NativeModulePolyfill, ProcessPolyfill\n- SharedProcessProxy\n\nWind's polyfill files now act as re-export proxies, maintaining import path compatibility for existing consumers while directing them to the canonical implementation in Output. Fixes to polyfills should now be made in Output, not in Wind.",
			"SHA": "690304cb6c64d653ac5d7a1f93137d973424f139"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T17:10:30Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1049,
				19
			],
			"Message": "fix(Wind): Route colon-prefixed IPC methods through MountainIPCInvoke\n\nColon-prefixed method names (e.g., `file:write`, `shared_process:invoke`) cannot be registered as direct Tauri commands because Rust function names cannot contain colons. These methods must route through Mountain's single `MountainIPCInvoke` command, which unwraps the params back into the positional `Vec<Value>` that internal handlers consume.\n\nThis fix adds the routing logic to all Wind polyfills that invoke Tauri:\n- ChildProcessPolyfill, FileProtocolShim, FileSystemPolyfill\n- IPCRendererShim, NativeModulePolyfill, ProcessPolyfill\n- SharedProcessProxy\n\nAlso updates TauriIPC.ts to use the consistent PascalCase form `\"MountainIPCInvoke\"` (matching all other call sites in Wind/Sky/Output) instead of the snake-case form. Minor style fixes in LifecycleService and PostHog/Fallback comments (em dash → hyphen).\n\nAll colon-prefixed IPC calls in Wind now route correctly through Mountain.",
			"SHA": "039f52cd9f8b0a41523b7d96c4e4f5d0d154b229"
		}
	],
